WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:04.720
Captain America, Iron Man, Thor, Hulk, Black
Widow, and Hawkeye.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.430
These six heroes have led the charge within
the Marvel Cinematic Universe for more than

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.860
ten years and twice as many movies.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.980
And with Avengers Endgame bringing them all
together again, it seems fitting to go over

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.000
each of their story arcs leading up to this
epic crescendo.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.720
Of course, trying to watch every MCU movie
in a row is a nearly two-day-long endeavor

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.230
at this point, so we've gone ahead and condensed
each original Avenger's story for you: here's

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.360
how each Avenger got to Endgame.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.100
The MCU got its start when Iron Man arrived
in theaters in 2008.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.710
Robert Downey Jr.'s impressive performance
introduced us to a narcissistic Tony Stark

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:42.840
who was used to having things his own way…
until he got kidnapped by the Ten Rings and

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.760
had to build his first Iron Man suit to regain
his freedom.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.559
From there he etched his name into the Marvel
hall of fame by helping stop threats such

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.940
as Iron Monger, Whiplash, the Chitauri invasion
of New York, Aldrich Killian, and Ultron.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.070
But Stark's true arc always focused on his
own inner struggle as he came to grips with

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.480
who he was without his "tricks and toys."

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.720
Once just a billionaire playboy, the man has
slowly evolved into a thoughtful, caring hero.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.580
His loyalty to Pepper Potts and father figure
status to Peter Parker are excellent examples

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.140
of how he's matured over time.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.260
And then there's the role he's played in setting
the stage for the Thanos epic.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.040
His prophetic vision in Age of Ultron gave
him a unique sense of urgency that continued

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.520
to fuel him as he tried to prepare for the
Mad Titan's impending arrival.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.060
Thanos clearly had an affinity with the Iron
Avenger, too, as shown through his assertion

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.570
that they were both "cursed with knowledge"
during Infinity War, leaving a potential showdown

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.260
between the two in Endgame a positively tantalizing
prospect.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.140
While Hulk has been a bit of an enigma throughout
the MCU thus far, his story can basically

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.180
be broken down into three eras.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.680
First, we have his solo film, which came out
after Iron Man.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.540
It showcased Bruce Banner, then played by
Edward Norton, already on the run, in love

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.500
with Betty Ross, and relentlessly pursued
by her father.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:01.400
The film ended with Banner having more or
less come to terms with "the Other Guy."

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.200
The second era opened up when Mark Ruffalo
picked up the mantle in Avengers.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.119
Banner and the Green Machine seemed to have
taken a few steps back at that point, as neither

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.980
wanted to surrender control to the other.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.540
The duo continued to help the Avengers for
a while afterward, and sparks even began to

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.400
fly between Banner and Black Widow in Age
of Ultron.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.590
But it all came to a screeching halt when
Hulk took over at the end of the movie and

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.360
flew the Quinjet into space.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.400
The third era began when Hulk showed up two
years later in Thor: Ragnarok, beginning a

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.900
three-movie character arc.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.480
This new story continued as Hulk remained
out of sight throughout most of Infinity War.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.580
The end of the three-part story will take
place in Endgame, with some sort of climactic

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.880
event likely in store for the Jade Giant.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.680
Black Widow has proven to be an absolutely
invaluable addition to the team over the years.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.150
She first appeared in Iron Man 2, already
trained as an accomplished spy and assassin

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.300
working for S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.360
She showed up again in Avengers and played
a critical role in ending the Battle of New

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.780
York when she closed the portal with Loki's
Scepter.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:04.220
She went on from there to help topple HYDRA's
infiltration of S.H.I.E.L.D and bring Ultron

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.300
down in Sokovia.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.920
She turned heads yet again when she switched
sides to join Team Cap in Civil War, helping

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.940
Captain America and Bucky Barnes escape in
the Quinjet.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.959
She re-emerged with Cap and company in the
early minutes of Infinity War and made her

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.220
presence known throughout the fight in Wakanda.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.080
Black Widow has been featured heavily in the
Endgame trailers and seems likely to be right

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.160
by Cap's side when the action picks up again.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.280
Thor has enraptured fans since the moment
Mjolnir was seen in the end credits scene

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.320
of Iron Man 2.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.010
The Son of Odin kicked things off on a low
note in Thor by being sent into exile after

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.180
he disobeyed his father.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.430
However, by the end of the movie, he had grown
into a character that appreciated the seriousness

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.920
of his responsibilities as a prince of Asgard.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.420
After his opening film, he provided some serious
muscle for the Avengers in the Battle of New

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:49.920
York.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.300
He then flew off to stop the Dark Elf Malekith
from wiping out the entire universe in his

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.560
second solo adventure.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.280
From there he doubled back to Earth, where
he helped stop Ultron and conducted some preliminary

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.900
Infinity Stone research.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.260
However, the character truly hit his stride
in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.320
The humor-infused capstone to Thor's trilogy
brought a whole new angle to the Asgardian

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.230
as he struggled with the loss of his father,
took down his sister, and ultimately took

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.200
up his kingship.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.600
The movie also set the stage for Infinity
War, which opened with many of the surviving

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.000
Asgardians being wiped out by Thanos.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.060
During Infinity War, Thor's character arc
reached an electrifying conclusion as he forged

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:31.099
Stormbreaker, summoned the Bifrost on his
own, and even managed to land what looked

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.780
like a fatal blow against Thanos.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:37.600
It's no understatement to say that the King
of Asgard enters Endgame ready for a rematch.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.900
Much like Natasha Romanoff, Clint Barton has
made an MCU living off cameos and supporting

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.380
roles, and his lack of superpowers naturally
puts him at a disadvantage.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.650
But that's never done much to stop the arrow-wielding
hero from making his mark.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.980
Hawkeye made his first appearance in Thor
as an agent of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:58.880
He showed up again in Avengers, when Loki
possessed him with the Mind Stone.

00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:03.060
Once he was freed from the Asgardian's influence,
however, he was quick to join the Avengers

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.180
in their successful defense of New York City.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:09.720
From there, his path led to Age of Ultron,
when he brought the refugee Avengers to his

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.640
family's home.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:15.140
The revelation that Barton was, at heart,
a family man brought a new dimension to the

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:15.640
character.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.200
After the mess in Sokovia, Barton retired
from the Avengers only to be drawn back into

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.180
the fray by Cap during Civil War.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.080
The whole affair ended with him under house
arrest.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.280
During the scene at the Avengers HQ in Infinity
War, Black Widow reminded the Avengers, and

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.520
the audience, about his current legal status:

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.280
"Where's Clint?"

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.900
"After the whole accords situation, he and
Scott took a deal.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.880
It was too tough on their families, they're
on house arrest."

00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:43.180
While he may have sat out for the first half
of the two-part epic, the trailers for Endgame

00:05:43.189 --> 00:05:47.580
have revealed that chances are good we'll
see quite a bit more Barton, this time likely

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.860
under the guise of Ronin.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.520
While it may seem hard to believe, Steve Rogers
was the last of the big six to make his entrance

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.660
into the MCU.

00:05:55.849 --> 00:06:00.420
His first solo movie, coming right before
Avengers, traced Rogers' path from a rejected

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.680
military recruit to the super soldier Captain
America.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:09.139
After stopping Red Skull in his origin film,
Cap went on to save the world again in Avengers,

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.220
becoming the heart and soul of the superhero
team.

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:17.520
Next, Cap teamed up with Black Widow and Sam
Wilson, a.k.a. Falcon, to take down a HYDRA-infiltrated

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.780
S.H.I.E.L.D. in Captain America: Winter Soldier.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.860
From there he led the Avengers into their
battle against Ultron in the second Avengers

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:24.360
installment.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:29.300
In Civil War, he chose to defend Bucky Barnes,
put his shield through Iron Man's chest armor,

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.789
and was forced to go into hiding.

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:35.540
He re-emerged from exile in Infinity War after
being informed of Thanos' imminent arrival.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.800
There's no doubt that Cap is more than capable
of holding his own in a fight.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.820
But, much like Tony Stark, his true journey
so far has revolved around his inner struggles.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.339
Over time he's shifted from a shining beacon
of national hope to a fugitive on the run

00:06:49.339 --> 00:06:51.349
from the very government that created him.

00:06:51.349 --> 00:06:55.830
No matter how bad things have gotten, Steve
Rogers has never lost his ability to follow

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:59.960
his moral compass, a fact that will certainly
play into his decisions in Endgame.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:04.420
While the six founding Avengers have all had
their own personal story arcs throughout the

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:09.680
first three phases of the MCU, the story of
their alliance as a team of Earth's mightiest

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.060
heroes has also played a prominent role
in the lead-up to Endgame.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:17.580
Thanks to Captain Marvel, we now know that
Nick Fury was given the idea to create the

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.919
"Protector Initiative" in the mid-'90s after
seeing how real the threat of an intergalactic

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:22.919
invasion could be.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.279
Of course, he fittingly renamed it the "Avengers
Initiative," creating the famous name for

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:31.600
the superhero squad, after he saw that it
was Danvers' call sign in the Air Force.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.039
The first Avengers featured Director Fury
as he assembled the Avengers to face the threat

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:37.529
of Loki and the Mind Stone.

00:07:37.529 --> 00:07:42.180
Sure, the team had a few early issues, but
you can't gather that many eccentrically powerful

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:45.900
personalities into a single group without
expecting some kind of friction.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:49.680
Besides, who doesn't want to watch Thor take
on the Hulk in a helicarrier?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:53.569
But after getting over those growing pains,
they meshed together beautifully as they took

00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:58.819
on Loki, bottled up the Chitauri hordes in
NYC, and sent a nuke as a parting gift before

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:00.340
closing up the invasion portal.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.080
As the credits rolled, the team looked good
enough to eat.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.900
Y'know, like, at a table:

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:14.720
Almost an entire phase after the first Avengers
movie, its sequel, Avengers: Age of Ultron,

00:08:14.729 --> 00:08:15.839
arrived in theaters.

00:08:15.839 --> 00:08:19.529
The Battle of New York spooked Tony Stark
enough to begin working on what he called

00:08:19.529 --> 00:08:24.020
the Ultron Program, which was meant to protect
the world from future global threats.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.300
Of course, the whole experiment went horribly
wrong when they introduced the Mind Stone

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.800
to the equation, inadvertently creating Ultron
in the process.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.800
Age of Ultron provided an opportunity for
the team to grow, while also introducing classic

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.460
Silver Age characters Scarlet Witch and Vision.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.300
Both characters have become Avenger staples
since, and are even getting their own miniseries.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:49.380
Ultron also served as a launchpad for Thanos
and the Infinity Stones to move toward center

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:49.880
stage.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.600
After their high point in Avengers, the next
chapter of the group's history would be shadowed

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.680
by internal friction.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:09:00.420
As if Ultron wasn't bad enough, just a couple
of movies later the Avengers turned on each

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.480
other in Captain America: Civil War.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.980
With Hulk and Thor both out of the picture,
the third installment of Cap's trilogy saw

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:11.300
the rest of the gang fall out hard after an
operation went south, leading to civilian

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.850
casualties and a public relations nightmare.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:19.080
The event sparked the demand for the Avengers
to sign the Sokovia Accords, which were designed

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.380
to provide a measure of government control
over superpowered vigilantes.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.920
Split over whether to sign the Accords or
not, Tony Stark and Steve Rogers rallied the

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:31.630
Avengers into two separate groups before duking
it out during the famous airport battle in

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.120
Leipzig.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:36.420
The story ended with Rogers and company on
the lam, with the rest of the Avengers either

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.040
technically operating under government control
or under house arrest.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.820
Needless to say, it was a low point for the
team.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:47.820
The next time the entire team was seen in
action was when Thanos showed up, and the

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.660
results were anything but pretty.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:54.000
Infinity War began with the Mad Titan and
his minions embarking on their quest for the

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.690
Infinity Stones in earnest, and for much of
the movie, the Avengers were scattered across

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:02.160
the galaxy, all fighting to the best of their
ability on their own.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:06.860
While several team members were able to provide
a united front in Wakanda, and Iron Man and

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:11.000
Spider-Man were able to team up with Doctor
Strange and the Guardians of the Galaxy on

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:15.460
Titan, Thanos ended up having relatively minimal
trouble getting through each of the groups

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:15.960
separately.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:20.660
As the Infinity War credits rolled, Tony Stark
was stranded on the other side of the solar

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.960
system, with the remaining Avengers wallowing
in the dust back on Earth.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:29.240
The questions that remain going forward are
if, how, and when the team will finally reassemble,

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:33.420
for the first time since the end of Phase
2, to take on Thanos with a finally united

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:33.960
front.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:39.640
In an interview with Empire Magazine, Marvel
boss Kevin Feige explained just how important

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:44.000
Endgame is as a capstone for the entire first
three phases of the MCU.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:44.960
He explained:

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:49.440
"We wanted to bring to a conclusion a series
of movies in a way that had never been done

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:49.940
before.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.760
Harry Potter had an ending because there were
only so many books.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.080
Lord of the Rings too.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:58.820
But we thought, 22 movies in, wouldn't it
be fun to bring some finality to the storyline?"

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:03.030
The knowledge that the creators themselves
see Endgame as a sort of capstone for the

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:08.100
first three phases of Marvel movies is reason
enough to expect that the Avengers, particularly

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:12.300
the central six that have been so focused
on so far, will play critical roles.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:16.700
The fact that they were all left standing,
along the heavy focus on them in the promotional

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:20.930
material for Endgame, seems to imply that
the "Infinity Saga" that started with the

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.660
founding Avengers will end with them as well.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:28.660
While the Infinity Saga may be drawing to
a close, the sky's the limit for the Marvel

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:32.040
Cinematic Universe as the studio moves forward
from Endgame.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:36.320
At this point, a whole new batch of potential
Avenger material is available in the form

00:11:36.329 --> 00:11:40.900
of newer characters like Spider-Man, Black
Panther, and the newest member of them all,

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:41.440
Captain Marvel.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:46.080
In addition, there's the boatload of A-list
Marvel characters brought into the fold thanks

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.460
to the Disney/Fox merger.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:52.040
The point is, Marvel has a lot to work with,
and the abundance of options opens up the

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.550
possibility for Endgame to be more than a
long-awaited reunion of old friends saving

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:57.800
the world yet again.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:02.820
While it's sad to think of going into Phase
4 without all of the original Avengers around,

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:06.620
there's no doubt that their influence will
continue to be felt for years to come.

